# The Rohonc Codex

A reading edition: what the manuscript says, in English, read against the books it is compiled from. Book Two prints every folio's own text, line for line, and is the evidence.

## I. The Fall of Lucifer, and the Life of Adam and Eve

### folios 004v–006v

In the beginning there was the Lord God, and the earth. The sun and the moon, as the scripture says. Elijah the prophet. The angel of God said: the forefather, before the heart of man. The Father; Adam bowed down before the Lord. God in heaven eternal, and the brethren. Many angels; and God the Father had many angels about him. Among the angels, two hundred and fifty years and seven before the heart of man. The Father, Adam, and the angels; there was Lucifer, and the other angels. And the angels prayed, and for forty days and forty nights Lucifer among the brethren, in hell. And again the angel said to Elijah: Elijah, when there is as Lucifer, who did this — Lucifer, when he was seated on the throne of God the Father. God the Father went. (004v)

The angel of the Father said; God the Father; the angel said to Lucifer: because the cup was hidden away above of the Father, on the throne. And then God; the angel; Lucifer; the cup was hidden away above the Lord on the throne; and when the cup of Lucifer was hidden away, the angel returned to the Father. And then the angel, the Lord, the cup, Lucifer; the cup was hidden away above, and the other went. God the Father; the angel of the Father spoke to Lucifer; Lucifer said: because the cup was hidden away above with the Father, on the throne; and when Lucifer went to God, the angel said: God; the angel; the cup was hidden away above the Lord on the throne; and when the cup of Lucifer was hidden away, and then it was hidden. The angel returned, the angel, to God the Father, because there was said Lucifer; to the Lord; hidden; the Lord God; the mother to the Lord, to the Lord, this hidden. The angel, proud Lucifer, he on the throne; and then God, the angel, the Lord. The cup of Lucifer; the cup was hidden away above, said Lucifer to the Lord: hidden. (004r)

The mother of the Lord God was born; and Lucifer spoke to the Lord, to the Lord; Lucifer set himself upon the throne, equal to the Lord God. There was the earth; and then God the Father eternal, and Michael. The angels, faithful servants, rose up; and when they had risen, the heavenly ones spoke. God the Father eternal went to Lucifer, and Lucifer fell from the throne of the Lord; and when, within, they bowed down — and of the angels every one — to whom Lucifer would not bow. And then God the Father eternal saw it, and cried out. God the Father eternal: Lucifer departed by commandment, because all were angels to whom Lucifer bowed. And he refused, said God the Father, and he departed. This was the angel. He left food, and three said the angel to Elijah the prophet: Elijah, say that God the Father is. To the Son came the Holy Spirit. Father, Son, heart of man; and then God the Father, the Holy Spirit — how man knows the image of the Father. (002r)

The Son, the Spirit, heart; and then the Son, in the image of the Lord. Heart and likeness man is; all one; to the Father, the Son, the Spirit. Father, Son and Spirit took man, and every living creature. The soul heard. Adam saw the living, truly, not many; Father and Son — not many; the Holy Spirit; but this Lord is all, one God. And then God, the angel, Elijah the prophet. Elijah the prophet, when there were Father, Son and Spirit, going forth, and the brethren, in this world. Paradise the Lord God, Adam heart slime of the earth; and then Adam was heart, as was said before, slime of the earth, and became; he breathed into Adam, and he became living, and the Lord God took Adam, and Adam went into Paradise; and all heart. End of chapter. Adam. (002v)

The Lord God spoke to Adam. He took him, and every living thing was truly without hunger and thirst upon Adam, and no living thing died. There shall be sin, hunger, and thirst to him whom afterward the Lord took. To Adam, all was truly one. This law, this yoke, was laid upon Adam by commandment: you shall not eat of it, and on the day you eat of it you shall die. Adam would die. And then Adam slept within, and then upon him first, from the Holy Spirit, the Holy Spirit came within into Paradise, into the garden, and the Lord God took Adam's rib, and the heart said to the angel: your mother. And then Adam from it. (003r)

Bone of bone; and the two souls are one. Before this the angel said it, and the Lord God departed. And Eve went into Paradise; and when Eve came to that tree which stood in the midst, which the Lord God had by commandment forbidden, she saw a serpent in that tree, which stood in the midst by the Lord God's commandment. And then this serpent spoke of this fruit, and then Eve ate, because Adam, the Master, had by commandment forbidden it. And then this serpent Eve ate it, and Adam ate one of this fruit; and the fruit was one, and Adam ate; and Adam knew. (003v)

They knew evil and good, as the Lord God knows. And then they plucked the fruit, the serpent, this fruit, this serpent. And the day took it, and it took the fruit. Adam. And then the two of them, Adam, were naked. Adam saw it; and then Adam was ashamed. And chapter six: the angel of God said to Elijah. Elijah; and this deadly sin afterward was Lucifer's, the Father's. Lucifer had fallen from the eternal Father, and the brethren in hell. And seven said the angel of God to Elijah the prophet: Elijah, the Lord God departed from the eternal within Paradise, saying. (001r)

The Lord God, with the angels, came out and then departed. The Lord God from the eternal came within into Paradise, and then the Lord God said: Where are you? Adam. The Lord God spoke with his own mouth. Adam hid himself. Adam, who has done this? Said the Lord God: Where are you, Adam? Eve gave the food, and ate. The Lord God spoke heavenly, and then Eve answered to the Lord, and then the Lord God said: Why, Eve? Eve answered: I have done it. And then the Lord God said: Why, Eve? You have done it. And then: The serpent, it ate. And then the Lord God said to Adam: one commandment. This Adam did not keep the commandment. (001v)

Adam was, and to him who asked why, the gates were. Adam was of the earth, till the earth. He wanted to eat, and to grab, and it was through pine; and it was painful. What is coming shall be; and this evil—this evil is cursed. The earth shall slide and make room for evil. Man was made, all of this. The serpent dies; and the Lord God turned among Adam and Eve; and the Lord God went, and the angel with fire, and a sword; and out of Paradise he drove them, and set an angel with a sword within. (007r)

Cherubim were created within Paradise; but the angel, and then the Lord God with the angel, spoke from the table, and from eight. Elijah, the angel of God: Elijah, when the Lord God drove Adam out from Paradise; and then Eve dwelt in the field many years; and Adam had by Eve offspring, these two sons. And the firstborn was Cain, and the second was Abel. The third was Seth. And then Adam was blind in both eyes; and then Adam went into Paradise, the son; and this son was Cain, the son Abel, of Adam. And then Adam said: bring Adam from the tree of mercy. (007v)

A branch. And then the branch carried anointed through the light; and then by that light anointed, through the eye, blind Adam sees; and Adam was made whole. And then Seth went to the gate of Paradise; and to Seth appeared God’s angel, the angel of God, to Seth; and he went. Seth said: Adam my father. Seth went into Paradise when it was Adam his father. Seth brought from the tree of mercy a branch. Adam his father was, through sin; and Adam said, Adam, when Seth brought seed anointed through the light; and then by that light anointed, through the eye, the blind man sees; and Adam was made whole. And then the angel truly spoke; and then the angel went into Paradise, and Seth carried the branch. (006r)

Out of Paradise, from the tree, Adam was, through sin. And then the angel gave this branch; and then the branch he carried to his father Adam. And then he went into a city, and the city was where Adam was, a house. And then he came and knew the way; and within, all from the city knew the way; and out of the city one road; and then Seth went, and within knew the way; and then Seth said, one: oh, the Father, the Spirit, the Father knows Adam. And Adam was blind in both eyes—Adam, who was the Lord God’s, cast out of Paradise by the angel; and then the gospel, and they found years; and (006v)

## II. From the Flood to the House of David

### folios 008r–015v

And then, at that time, the Lord God appeared to Noah. And the Lord God was grieved that he had made man, because of the flood, and Noah kept his commandment. The Lord God would have all destroyed. The Lord God said to Noah: make one ark. It was forty cubits long, and broad; and five lifted up. Noah took of every creature two by two, and brought them inside of the ark. And then the dove went from the Lord. And Noah took of every creature two by two, and went before the Lord God; and to the cup, and to the Lord he lost himself and was drunken before the Lord God; all, two by two, in every direction. And the rain came for forty days; and five cities were destroyed. The Lord God was with Noah. The angel of God said to Elijah: the Lord God was with Noah. Noah remained through all this; and the other sons departed. (008r)

The people were pagans and believed until Abraham the forefather. From Noah it was, until Abraham. The angel of God said to Elijah the prophet: Elijah, believe within this and that. One man was saved in that time. The angel departed from before Elijah the prophet; and this and that he said. Elijah the prophet wrote; and holy Enoch within one chapter of the writing. (008v)

And the son went with the father; and a sheep, and a lamb. The father sacrificed the son; the father Abraham, for love of the Lord, made the offering to the Lord God. And then Isaac was tied up, and there was a ram instead of Isaac. Abraham sacrificed, and drew out Isaac, whom he would slay; and the Lord God cried out from the cloud, by the angel of the Lord God, to Abraham. Abraham loved the Lord. This is peace to the Lord. And then he looked up and saw, Abraham, and saw a lamb in a thornbush. (005r)

And then he sacrificed the lamb; and the Lord God from the cloud, by the angel of the Lord, said to Abraham: a holy Virgin; of a virgin shall be born a son. The son shall be Jesus; and the Lord went among the people. He preached the gospel, did many miracles, and the Lord suffered crucified; and on the third day rose from the dead. The Lord God, by the angel, said to Abraham: believe truly in the Son of the living God; every man is saved. One man, but every man is saved from the yoke; and man believes in the Lord. But every man was damned, from Adam onward until Abraham, a hundred years and twenty years; from Abraham until Moses began: three thousand and fifty from Abraham until. (005v)

Afterward David the king humbled himself before the Lord. The king began his repentance; afterward the king was anointed. Have mercy; and the king's sin — have mercy. At that time there appeared to the king the angel of God; the angel of God said to David the king: the Lord God. The king sinned; have mercy. The king keeps the Lord's commandment; and the Lord confirmed the king upon the king's throne; and the king proclaimed it to the people. The Lord said, a son shall be born of David; the son shall be the Son of God. And the angel departed from before David. From David the king until the Virgin Mary, and one, and one, and one, six, and five, from David the king until the Virgin Mary. (015r)

The birthday: from Adam onward until the Virgin Mary was born, years: five thousand and one hundred years and fifty and four years, and four years. (015v)

Saint Luke writes; the sixth part of his writing. They gave thanks, and prayed to the Lord God. (016r)

And Saint Anne; of the two of them, all their rich substance they divided into parts. One portion they gave to the people of the temple; and a second portion to the Lord, as a way for the people. A third portion they kept for themselves. And all Joachim's household gave thanks to the Lord God; and his household had been together thirty years; and he prepared the offering. And then, from Joachim he brought his offering; and the chief of the Jews looked at Joachim. This chief of the Jews said to Saint Joachim, to this Joachim, who was without children: Go among the people with the offering. And he cast Joachim out at this. And sorrowfully Joachim departed, and went into the field, into the wilderness, and from there to a place. (016v)

## III. Joachim and Anne, and the Birth of Christ

### folios 016r–022r

A lamb was brought for sacrifice, and the sacrifice was rejected. At that time Joachim was in the desert, and the angel of God came to Joachim and said, Hear me. The angel of God said to Joachim, The Lord God has had mercy. Go home, Joachim; and at the golden gate — and Joachim departed — Joachim's wife Anne conceived a virgin maiden. And the virgin maiden shall be Mary; and Mary shall bear a son. The son shall be Jesus; and the Lord went among the people. He preached the gospel, did many miracles, and suffered, the Lord crucified; and on the third day rose from the dead; and his rising shall save every wide world, and the man who believes in the Lord. And the angel departed from before Saint Joachim; and at that time the angel appeared. (017r)

The angel of God came to Saint Anne and said, Anne, the Lord God has had mercy and has heard you. Go home, Anne; and at the golden gate Anne came to the Lord's Joachim; and there was conceived a virgin maiden. And then the virgin maiden was born in the body — she is Mary; and Mary shall bear a son, and his name — the son shall be, in the body, Jesus; and the Lord went out; he preached the gospel, did many miracles; and the Lord suffered crucified; and on the third day from death the Lord rose; and his rising saves every wide people, and the man who believes in the Lord. And the angel departed from before Saint Anne; and there was conceived the blessed Virgin Mary. And Mary carried the child nine months, and in the tenth the child was born; and this was two months; and at six years from Adam onward until the Virgin Mary was conceived and born: five thousand one hundred and fifty. (017v)

Months passed until the offering of the blessed Virgin Mary. And then Mary was within; from the beginning she withdrew into hiding, and said that Mary would keep her virginity in her heart. O! O! Amen. And then Mary was six years old; and at that time God the Father in heaven saw all the darkness, and at that time God the Father in heaven sent the Lord's angel Gabriel to the blessed Virgin. Saint Luke writes in his writing: at that time the angel said, Gabriel: Hail, virgin, maiden full of grace! The Lord God is with Mary. And this virgin maiden said, How shall this be? This maiden does not know man; this maiden would keep her virginity. O! O! Amen. The angel Gabriel said to Mary. (018r)

The Holy Spirit shall come upon you, and grace to all. This maiden shall conceive a son; and the son shall be called Jesus. And then the blessed Virgin Mary said this; and the power of the Lord overshadowed her; and then the maiden answered, the Virgin Mary: the word of command to the Lord; Mary said, Be it done to me according to the word which the angel said. At this the Holy Spirit came upon the Virgin Mary, and the Lord Jesus Christ was conceived, Christ. And then the angel Gabriel departed from the Virgin Mary, and said to Mary: Behold, your kinswoman is six months gone, who conceived a son — Saint John. The Lord God's mercy to this: from John shall be the way made for the Lord Jesus Christ, that is the Lord whom Mary bore; and the Lord went forth; he preached the gospel. (018v)

And the Lord suffered under the Jews, crucified; and the man who believes in the Lord truly believes in the Son of the living God. Every man is saved, and one man is damned; and the Lord does not believe, and one is saved, but he who does not believe, a man is damned. Here ends this holy gospel.

And at that time the angel appeared, the angel of God, to the aged Joseph. And then the angel of God spoke to the very old Joseph: Go, aged one, Joseph, within to Mary. And this Joseph was already aged, of the son, well-pleasing, from Mary. And then the son shall be born; the son shall be Jesus. And the Lord went forth among the people; he preached the gospel, did many miracles, and the Lord suffered death. (019r)

And the man who believes in the Lord truly believes in the Son of the living God. Every man is saved, and one man is damned; and the Lord does not believe, and one is saved, but he who does not believe, a man is damned. Here ends this holy gospel.

And then the blessed Virgin Mary was sixteen years old. There was a decree, before the coming of the Lord Jesus Christ, twenty-two years; and one year before the coming of the Lord Jesus Christ. At that time Augustus the emperor commanded that all people should be counted. And then the law of Augustus the emperor sent all the world back. And then the two, Mary and aged Joseph, went home. And then the two, Mary and aged Joseph, took one ox and one. (019v)

Because this they took, aged Joseph the ox, the two of them — aged Joseph and Mary. They remained together, the two of them, the aged; and the donkey was aged Joseph's. He took her who would bear this son; Mary and aged Joseph carried her on the donkey. And then aged Joseph, when he arrived, aged Mary and Joseph, at Bethlehem town. And they found none; but the two of them, Mary and aged Joseph, lodged in a barn; and a manger. And then Joseph bought hay; and then the ox and the donkey; he laid the hay. (020r)

And then a fire began to give light; and then, over his shoulder, in the night the son was born; and the son was Jesus. At that time a sky star shone through Bethlehem town; and then a star was seen; and at the star, a miracle. At that time the angel said: Joy! A king is born, a king born in Bethlehem town, within a barn, in a donkey's manger. The donkey loved the hay within. Christ, Mary's son. And then they went to Bethlehem; and then they rejoiced and knelt down, and every one of them knelt before the shepherds, and hastened to go one after another. (020v)

Saint Luke writes inside one writing a chapter of the book, that from Adam onward until the birth of the Lord Jesus Christ was five thousand one hundred and sixty years, and six years, until the birth of the Lord Jesus Christ. (021r)

At that time, in the year the Lord Jesus Christ was born, three days after, the angel said to the aged Joseph: Rise up, and take this son and his mother, and flee into Egypt. And they went, all of them, beginning by night, out of Egypt into this; the angel said, day, Herod. Here ends this holy gospel. At that time he rose up, and took the Lord Jesus Christ and his mother, and five years, when they went into Jerusalem, that is, when the Lord Jesus Christ was born. On the eighth day the son was circumcised, and the son was named Jesus. And this Lord Jesus first shed his blood; and then the Lord Jesus was circumcised in Jerusalem. Chapter. And they fled, Mary his mother, the Holy Spirit, and Joseph. (021v)

They went into the land of Egypt, and dwelt there; and the Lord went with Joseph in the land of Egypt, into every city. The idols, the evil ones, pierced and pierced; and they died. From Joseph they remained in Egypt twelve years. At that time the angel Gabriel said to Joseph: Flee into the land of Egypt, into Nazareth city. And they remained in that city twelve years; and this was thirty-one years. Here ends this holy gospel. He called twelve apostles; and many miracles afterward: the blind eye the Lord gave light; the dead the Lord resurrected; the evil among the people he cast out. (022r)

First, that is, the Lord made water wine. That is, the Lord broke five loaves of bread for the people. The fourth sign the Lord Jesus showed, when he raised up a son. The fifth sign the Lord Jesus showed, when he raised up the lost in Jerusalem. The sixth sign the Lord Jesus showed, when the Jews brought a sick man before the Lord Jesus: a sick man, and a sick man, and a sick man, and a paralytic; and the sick, the sick, the sick, the paralytic — the Lord Jesus healed them. The seventh sign the Lord Jesus showed in Capernaum, when he healed alive the servant of a soldier; and the centurion was named. The eighth sign the Lord Jesus showed in Tyre, to a woman. (022v)

## IV. The Twelve Signs of His Coming

### folios 022v–028v

A pagan had a devil within her, and the Lord cast it out of her. The ninth sign the Lord Jesus showed in a proud paralytic man, because of what the man did. The tenth sign the Lord Jesus showed in a king’s son, because he was at the point of death; and afterward the son lived. The eleventh sign the Lord Jesus showed in Jerusalem: the evil spirit, when the Lord cast a devil out of a man. First, before the birth of the Lord Jesus Christ, the Son of God cannot be known by a prophet or a forefather; but afterward he is Christ; and by miracle they confessed that the Lord Jesus is truly the Son of God. Five confessed the Lord Jesus, that the Lord Jesus is truly the Son of God. First confessed the Lord Jesus, Moses and Elijah. (023r)

Secondly confessed the Lord Jesus: God the Father, the Lord’s own. The evil ones confessed that the Lord Jesus is truly the Son of God. Fourthly confessed the Lord Jesus — the angels — that the Lord Jesus is truly the Son of God. They confessed; and the earth, the sun, and the moon, that the Lord Jesus is truly the Son of God; and all this, that the Lord Jesus is truly the Son of God. First confessed it Saint Peter, Moses and Elijah. Saint Luke writes that when the Lord Jesus was thirty years old, at that time the Lord Jesus went to Mount Tabor with his apostles; and he was transfigured; and the apostles saw Moses and Elijah white, and they saw the light; and then there stood the Lord Jesus, and Moses and Elijah; and then the apostles, through fear, fell down; and then the apostles heard this word spoken, beloved of the Son; and the Father’s voice; and then they were alone — not the apostles, and not everyone, but only the Lord Jesus. Here ends this holy gospel. Secondly confessed the Lord Jesus, God the Father: first on Mount Tabor, secondly on Mount Carmel. (023v-024r)

Because when the Lord Jesus was thirty years old, at that time the Lord Jesus went to be baptized by Saint John on Mount Carmel; and then the Lord went to Saint John. The Lord Jesus said: John. The Lord said to Saint John: Master, and I have come to be baptized. And the Lord Jesus said, John, baptize the Lord; and Saint John baptized the Lord Jesus, when the Lord was thirty years old; and the Holy Spirit appeared in the form of a dove, and then: This is the Lord’s Son, he on whom the Spirit came to rest; and the Lord took the Holy Spirit; and the Lord went into the field. (024r-024v)

The devils confessed that the Lord Jesus is truly the Son of God. When the Lord Jesus was thirty years old, he went into the town, and a man knelt down before him. The man had one son, and a devil was in him. The man’s son — the apostles could not heal him. He begged the Lord to heal this man’s son. The Lord Jesus said, “Have mercy; the lunatic son can be healed.” And then the son came before the Lord Jesus, and he was made whole. And these three confessed — the devils — that the Lord Jesus is truly the Son of God, because by miracle they confessed. Fourthly, the angels confessed the Lord Jesus at the birth of the Lord Jesus Christ, because the Lord Jesus was born in Bethlehem. (025r)

In the town, first, before the birth, there was a saying: a star through Bethlehem town. Then the star was seen by sons, and they rejoiced. And then at the star, a miracle. At that time the angel said to the shepherds, “Great joy! A king is born, a king born in Bethlehem town, in a barn, in a donkey’s manger, with the ox and the donkey, in the hay — Christ, Mary’s son.” And then they went to Bethlehem, and knelt down, and every one of them knelt. And then the sons hastened to go to one another, and gave thanks to the Most High Lord, and gave thanks. Here ends this holy gospel. (025v)

And the earth and the moon, because when the Lord Christ was crucified, the earth quaked, the rocks and the stones split. (026r)

The sun and the moon were darkened, and every tree in the world humbled itself, and all creation mourned when Christ was crucified. And all these five confessed in sorrow that the Lord Jesus is truly the Son of God; and by miracle they confessed that the Lord Jesus is truly the Son of God. And the Lord suffered under the Jews. The Lord God said to Abraham by the angel; and the Lord God said to the blessed Virgin Mary by the angel; and to holy, very old Joseph. And the man who believes in the Lord, that he is truly the Son of the living God — every man is saved; and a man who does not believe in the Lord is damned, and perishes. One is saved, but a man is damned. And this he said. First Abraham the forefather confessed it. Secondly holy Anne confessed. (026v)

The mother, the blessed Virgin Mary, confessed third. The angel of God said: at that time the Lord was; the Lord God went; the Lord's angel went to the blessed Virgin Mary, when out from the years to the house of the Virgin Mary she conceived; and she bore; and on the eighth day, and one hundred and sixteen years and five. At that time God the Father in heaven, because he saw all people in darkness under the sky. At that time God the Father in heaven; and the Lord's angel Gabriel went in to the blessed Virgin Mary, and said this and that. Saint Luke writes the chapter in his writing; and the man who believes in the Lord, that he is truly the Son of the living God — every man is saved; and one man is damned; and the Lord does not believe; and one is saved; but every man is damned; and thus he said. Saint Joseph the aged confessed it. The angel of God said, because the Lord God spoke by the angel Gabriel; and whosoever is the Lord's believes truly the Son of the living God — every man is saved; and one man is damned; and the Lord is saved, but every man is damned; and thus he said. The Lord Jesus spoke of his many wounds, when the Lord went to his death; and then the Lord was with the apostles in Jerusalem. At that time the Lord Jesus knelt before the blessed Virgin Mary; and the Lord Jesus said: there are not many gods but rather one God. And then the Lord Jesus, and the Lord in the Lord Jesus Christ; and one is saved, but every man is damned; and Mary blessed the Lord Jesus, with all the apostles — the blessed Virgin Mary. (027r-027v)

And then Mary kissed the Lord Jesus, the Lord's mother, the blessed Virgin Mary; and then Mary was, and Mary kissed her son the Lord Jesus Christ; and from Mary the Lord Jesus went to Bethany with the apostles in Jerusalem, because the apostles were at supper. Before the Lord went into Jerusalem, where the apostles were at supper, the apostles prepared a lamb, because at that time was the feast of the Jews, the Passover. There began the suffering of the Lord Jesus Christ, Son of God; because the Lord is truly the Son of God. And then the Lord, the Jews crucified; and then the Lord, the apostles, the mother; he was laid in the tomb, and rose from the dead. And the twelfth sign the Lord Jesus showed, when he rose from prayer and the Lord and the apostles appeared in Jerusalem; and the sign the Lord Jesus showed. (028r)

When he ascended into heaven on a mountain, two men and two men were exorcised of six hundred, and six thousand, and sixty, and six devils of hell, and the two men were healed afterward. The fourteenth sign the Lord Jesus showed; then when he went to God his Father in heaven; the Lord sat at the right hand of God the Father. (028v)

## V. The Passion

### folios 029r–052v

Here begins the account of the Passion of a man, the writing of the account of the Passion of Saint Matthew and Saint John, of the Passion. The Lord Jesus went to Bethany, to Jerusalem, because the Lord went to the supper. Before the Lord went, the apostles went into Jerusalem to prepare the Passover lamb, where the Lord and the apostles should eat. And the Lord said: go, you. And then the Lord spoke to the apostles in Jerusalem; and the Lord sat down at the table with the apostles. At that time the apostles prepared the Passover lamb; and the lamb the apostles brought to the table. The Lord Jesus said: I have wanted to eat this lamb with you before I suffer. Therefore the Lord asks you: do not, apostles, be offended in the Lord, because the Lord goes to his death — the Lord dies. And the Lord Jesus rose from the table, and laid aside his garments. The Lord Jesus, one apostle among the apostles, and among seven the apostles, and an apostle brought a bucket and a washing-dish; and then water into the dish he poured; and the Lord Jesus came to Saint Peter, and brought the water in the dish, which the Lord Jesus then brought to Saint Peter. (029r-029v)

Master, do not let the Lord wash my feet. And then the Lord Jesus said: if the Lord does not wash your feet, you have no part within heaven. And then Peter said: Master, not only my feet, but also my hands and my head. The Lord took the basin and washed them; and all of them he washed; and then the Lord washed their feet; and with the towel he wiped the feet of every one of the apostles, every one he washed; and the Lord Jesus took his garments again. (030r)

The Lord Jesus sat at table with the apostles and then the Lord Jesus looked at the apostles, to see how the Lord would give himself to you, and you shall eat. And the Lord Jesus took one baked loaf, and blessed the Lord Jesus this bread, and the Lord set it before them; and the Lord Jesus took wine in a cup, and poured water into the cup; and blessed the Lord Jesus the wine and the water; and the wine and water the Lord Jesus set before them. And then the Lord Jesus said: whoever eats of this bread, that man shall be called the Lord's; and the man who eats this bread. (030v)

He who eats and believes in the Lord, every man is damned; and the man who believes in the Lord and is from the Lord, they ate the holy Host and drank, that man shall live. O! O! Amen. And then the Lord Jesus knew: one among you, and the Lord said one of the apostles shall betray him. And the apostles looked among the apostles, saying, Master, who is it? And the Lord Jesus said; and leaning on the breast of the Lord Jesus with John, he said: O Master, who is it? And then he leaned upon the Lord Jesus. Master, thus said the Lord Jesus to whom; the Lord took a morsel. (031r)

It is he. And then he leaned upon the Lord Jesus; and he took this bread. Nicodemus saw the Lord Jesus give the morsel, this bread. And then Judas Iscariot took the bread; and then the eyes of Judas were opened. In that place the devil entered into Judas. The apostles wept for the Lord Jesus; and he took this from the Son of God, the Lord Jesus. Judas did what he did; and then the apostles wondered how he said: Master, speak. But the apostles did not understand what Judas said. He went to buy bread, because he was the shepherd, because the apostles thought this was the Jews' Passover. (031v)

And Judas went to the Jews' chief in Jerusalem, because the Lord was there. On Wednesday one of the apostles betrayed him — Judas — because he took for the Lord thirty pieces of silver. And then the Lord Jesus said to the Lord's brethren: the Lord goes to God his Father; and the Lord will send you the Holy Spirit; and you shall see that the Lord goes to his death. The Lord dies, because the Jews crucified the Lord; and the Lord on the third day shall rise again. Therefore the Lord asks you: do not, apostles, be offended in the Lord, because he goes to God his Father. (032r)

Peter said: Master — Peter would follow the Lord; the Lord dies. The Lord Jesus said to Peter: first, before the cock, you shall deny the Lord. And Peter said to the Lord Jesus: Peter, this shall not be. Therefore the Lord asks you: do not be offended in the Lord; because the apostles were very sorrowful for the Lord. And one of the Jews was a judge; and the mouth of the Lord Jesus said: but the Lord went on the way, because the Lord Jesus knew when the Lord would find Judas in the house of the high priest. And many miracles and much preaching afterward the Lord Jesus did on the way. (032v)

